---
const topics = [
  "SRE",
  "Platform Engineering",
  "Distributed Systems",
  "Observability",
  "AI & Automation",
];

const articles = [
  {
    category: "AI & AUTOMATION",
    title: "Who Verifies the AI Agent That Fixed Production?",
    description:
      "Autonomous remediation creates a new reliability problem: the system taking action shouldn't be the only system deciding whether that action worked.",
    readTime: "7 MIN READ",
  },
  {
    category: "OBSERVABILITY",
    title: "Telemetry Is Becoming the Context Layer for AI Operations",
    description:
      "Logs, metrics and traces aren't just for engineers anymore. They're becoming the context AI needs to reason about production systems.",
    readTime: "8 MIN READ",
  },
];
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="The Reliability Loop — ideas and deep dives on SRE, platform engineering, observability, distributed systems, AI and automation."
    />
    <title>The Reliability Loop</title>

    <style is:global>
      :root {
        --bg: #0b0d10;
        --surface: #11151a;
        --text: #f2f4f7;
        --muted: #9ca6b2;
        --line: #252b33;
        --accent: #7dd3fc;
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      html {
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--text);
        font-family:
          Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont,
          "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--bg);
      }

      a {
        color: inherit;
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      .container {
        width: min(1120px, calc(100% - 48px));
        margin: 0 auto;
      }

      header {
        height: 82px;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      }

      nav {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        align-items: center;
        width: 100%;
      }

      .brand {
        font-size: 14px;
        font-weight: 750;
        letter-spacing: 0.13em;
      }

      .nav-links {
        display: flex;
        gap: 32px;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 14px;
      }

      .hero {
        padding: 110px 0 90px;
      }

      .eyebrow {
        color: var(--accent);
        font-size: 12px;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.16em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        margin-bottom: 28px;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: clamp(52px, 7vw, 92px);
        letter-spacing: -0.055em;
        line-height: 0.97;
        max-width: 920px;
        margin: 0;
        font-weight: 650;
      }

      .hero-copy {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 20px;
        line-height: 1.7;
        max-width: 720px;
        margin-top: 38px;
      }

      .topics {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 10px;
        margin-top: 45px;
      }

      .topic {
        border: 1px solid var(--line);
        border-radius: 999px;
        padding: 9px 14px;
        color: #c5ccd5;
        font-size: 12px;
      }

      section {
        border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
        padding: 72px 0;
      }

      .section-label {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 11px;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.17em;
        margin-bottom: 34px;
      }

      .featured {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1.5fr 0.7fr;
        gap: 80px;
      }

      h2 {
        font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 62px);
        line-height: 1.05;
        letter-spacing: -0.04em;
        margin: 0;
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .featured-copy,
      .article-description {
        color: var(--muted);
        line-height: 1.7;
      }

      .featured-copy {
        font-size: 18px;
        margin-top: 28px;
        max-width: 690px;
      }

      .metadata {
        color: var(--accent);
        font-size: 11px;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      }

      .featured-side {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        justify-content: flex-end;
        gap: 14px;
        color: var(--muted);
      }

      .articles {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        gap: 70px;
      }

      .article {
        padding-right: 20px;
      }

      .article h3 {
        font-size: 28px;
        line-height: 1.2;
        letter-spacing: -0.025em;
        margin: 17px 0;
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .article-description {
        font-size: 15px;
      }

      .loop-section {
        text-align: center;
      }

      .loop {
        margin: 35px auto 0;
        max-width: 640px;
        padding: 40px;
        border: 1px solid var(--line);
        background: var(--surface);
        font-family: "SFMono-Regular", Consolas, monospace;
        color: #cbd5e1;
        line-height: 2.1;
        font-size: 14px;
      }

      .loop strong {
        color: var(--accent);
      }

      footer {
        border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
        padding: 45px 0;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 13px;
      }

      .footer-content {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
      }

      @media (max-width: 720px) {
        .container {
          width: min(100% - 32px, 1120px);
        }

        .hero {
          padding: 75px 0;
        }

        .nav-links {
          display: none;
        }

        .featured,
        .articles {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
          gap: 40px;
        }

        h1 {
          font-size: 52px;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <header>
      <nav class="container">
        <a class="brand" href="/">THE RELIABILITY LOOP</a>

        <div class="nav-links">
          <a href="#articles">Articles</a>
          <a href="#topics">Topics</a>
          <a href="#about">About</a>
        </div>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <div class="container">
        <div class="hero">
          <div class="eyebrow">Reliability Engineering / Field Notes</div>

          <h1>Engineering systems that survive reality.</h1>

          <p class="hero-copy">
            Ideas and deep dives on reliability engineering, distributed
            systems, observability, platform engineering and the emerging role
            of AI in production operations.
          </p>

          <div class="topics" id="topics">
            {topics.map((topic) => <span class="topic">{topic}</span>)}
          </div>
        </div>

        <section>
          <div class="section-label">FEATURED / 001</div>

          <div class="featured">
            <div>
              <div class="metadata">SRE · AI & AUTOMATION</div>

              <h2>From Automated Operations to Autonomous Reliability</h2>

              <p class="featured-copy">
                The next evolution of SRE isn't simply responding to incidents
                faster. It's deciding which parts of the incident lifecycle
                should require a human at all.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="featured-side">
              <span>Rahul Siddipeta</span>
              <span>9 min read</span>
              <span>October 2026</span>
              <span>Read article →</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="articles">
          <div class="section-label">LATEST FROM THE LOOP</div>

          <div class="articles">
            {
              articles.map((article) => (
                <article class="article">
                  <div class="metadata">{article.category}</div>
                  <h3>{article.title}</h3>
                  <p class="article-description">{article.description}</p>
                  <div class="metadata">{article.readTime} →</div>
                </article>
              ))
            }
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="loop-section">
          <div class="section-label">THE OPERATING MODEL</div>

          <h2>Reliability is a loop.</h2>

          <div class="loop">
            <strong>OBSERVE</strong>
            <br />↓<br />
            DETECT → UNDERSTAND → DECIDE
            <br />↑　　　　　　　　　　　↓<br />
            LEARN ← VERIFY ← ACT
            <br /><br />
            <strong>↻ REPEAT</strong>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </main>

    <footer id="about">
      <div class="container footer-content">
        <span>© 2026 The Reliability Loop</span>
        <span>Written by Rahul Siddipeta</span>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>